<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 24,274,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 24,274,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, meal exports in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 09/11/96    09/04/96     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 24,274,000  24,730,000   24,732,000</p>
<p> Capacity-X	33,990,000  33,990,000   33,842,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	34,637,015  34,637,015	    N/A</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  66,202     115,544	    N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may agree due to rounding by NOPA.  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   09/11/96    09/04/96    Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   4,247,000   4,493,000    4,768,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    4,373,000   4,654,000    4,285,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  3,760,000   3,618,000    4,398,000</p>
<p> South Central    2,152,000   2,554,000    1,877,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,338,000   3,639,000    2,940,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 4,833,000   3,947,000    4,618,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,572,000   1,824,000    1,846,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	24,274,000  24,730,000   24,732,000</p>
